WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.600
Narrator: Every venue has emergency plans - for fire, for security threats, for a power failure or bad weather.

2
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:13.200
Narrator: Who decides to evacuate? Not you, and not me.

3
00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:20.000
Narrator: The venue control room decides, together with Saudi Civil Defense and the Ministry of Interior.

4
00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.410
Narrator: Civil Defense command fire and evacuation.

5
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:32.110
Narrator: The Police lead security threats, including any evacuation for one.

6
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:40.310
Narrator: The Ministry of Interior and LOC Security carry out the evacuation, and we help them.

7
00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.710
Narrator: Your job: be ready, then act on the message.

8
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.750
Narrator: An evacuation can be local - one kiosk or room.

9
00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.450
Narrator: A sector - one stand.

10
00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.150
Narrator: Or, rarely, the full stadium.

11
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.750
Narrator: And sometimes the safest place is inside.

12
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:09.150
Narrator: Then you may be told to invacuate - move fans to safer areas inside - or that the stadium is locked down.

13
00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.850
Narrator: Same rule: follow the instruction.

